    "result_text": "The full suite (the acceptance tests plus base) is green: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `locality` field is a response-time derivation from `city`, so I followed the exact precedent already used for `membershipTier` (a derived getter on the `Owner` model, auto-mapped by MapStruct into the generated `OwnerDto`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `membershipTier`), documenting the fixed table and the `UNKNOWN` fallback. This makes the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` carry the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `getLocality()` method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table. MapStruct auto-maps it by name into the DTO, so it appears in both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor step was needed \u2014 like `membershipTier`, `locality` is a pure per-response derivation with nothing to persist, so a stored field or a pipeline step would have been redundant.\n\nBoth new tests pass: `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW`) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random `Town<seq>` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`).",
