    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change mirrors the derived read-only getter pattern already established in this class \u2014 the adjacent loyalty-tier method (`namesakeCount`/`\"SILVER\"`/`\"BRONZE\"`) computes a response-time value from the entity's own fields the same way, so `getLocality()` deriving from `this.city` sits in exactly the right unit and reads as natural to a maintainer here.\n\n- Logic is in the right place: `city` is an `Owner` field, and the region is a pure function of it, so a derived getter on `Owner` is the idiomatic home rather than a new service or DTO mapper.\n- No duplication: the table lives in a single `private static final Map`, and the OpenAPI `locality` schema documents the same rule at the API edge without re-encoding the mapping in code.\n- `Owner` is not becoming a catch-all \u2014 this is one small cohesive addition consistent with the existing derived-attribute getters, not an unrelated responsibility.\n- The Javadoc and `readOnly: true` schema entry keep the derivation self-documenting and additive.\n\nMinor (non-blocking) nit: the `CITY_REGION` constant is declared mid-class rather than with the other class fields at the top; matching the surrounding style of keeping the derived getter self-contained makes this defensible, so no change is required.",
